The bridge core (bridge.py, ops/, tests/, the inbox and long-task hooks,
and the executor manuals) comes from that project, implementing Tencent's
official openclaw-weixin (iLink Bot API) protocol.

Enhancements in this edition (2026-11, by the Cooper deployment):
  - hooks/wechat-window-reminder.* : a two-stage 24 h reply-window
    keep-alive reminder (a proactive nudge inside WeChat at <= 4 h left,
    then an App-side reminder at <= 60 min left or after the window closed).
  - install.sh : one-click deployment for the Muse (Hatch) runtime -
    relocates the tree to ~/workspace/wechat-bridge, installs Python
    dependencies into vendor/py (survives VM replacement), writes the
    service proxy env, installs the systemd unit and the hook scripts,
    then runs the test suite and the doctor.
  - DEPLOY.md : an agent-facing deployment runbook (hook registration,
    QR login flow, two-layer acceptance).
  - README.md : rewritten quick start and an enhancements section.

The MIT License terms of the original work continue to apply to the whole
combined work; the LICENSE file is preserved unmodified.
